{
  "_comment": "Header-guard table. Rule (RULES.md part F): normalise a header (lower case, every run of non-alphanumeric characters becomes one space, trim). A header whose normalised form equals a normalised TEMPLATE header always passes. Otherwise it is REFUSED when it contains any of the whole words cost, rate, postage, label, carrier, net, wholesale, negotiated, paid, invoice, buy (an optional plural s is allowed). The guard runs over every header of every sheet BEFORE anything is stored. A header that passes auto-maps to a money field only when it is an exact template money header, or it contains 'charged to' or 'billed to', or it contains the word customer together with one of charge, charges, charged, amount, fee, price, total; any other money-like header is left unmapped. The guard is best effort: no rule can prove that a number is customer-facing.",
